# A point S strictly between Q and R makes a triangle with P and Q where
# P, Q, R make one.
#
# With k = (R − S)/(Q − S) and x = (S − P)/(Q − P), (R − P)/(Q − P) is
# ((Q − S)/(Q − P))·k + x, and (Q − S)/(Q − P) is 1 − x; so x real would
# make (R − P)/(Q − P) real, which the triangle denies. S = P would make
# x = 0, real, so S is apart from P; it is apart from Q by being between.
